{{Quote|This is the lair of General Grievous.|Kit Fisto, to Nahdar Vebb|audio=LairOfGeneralGrievous-LoG.flac|<ref name="Lair of Grievous" />}}
'''Vassek 3''', also known as the '''third moon of Vassek''', was a [[moon]] of the [[planet]] [[Vassek]] located within the [[Vassek system]] of the region known as the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], the moon served as the location of the personal [[Grievous's fortress|fortress]] of the [[Kaleesh]] [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist Alliance]] [[General]] [[Grievous]]. In [[21 BBY]], during the war, [[Galactic Republic]] forces led by [[Jedi General]] [[Kit Fisto]] tracked the [[Rescue on the Tranquility|fugitive]] [[Trade Federation]] [[Viceroy]] [[Nute Gunray]] to Vassek 3. In the resulting [[Mission to Grievous's castle|engagement]] with Grievous, Fisto was forced to escape the moon as the lone Republic survivor.

==Description==
{{Quote|I know we're in the middle of nowhere, R6, but that's the Republic beacon we're looking for.|Kit Fisto, to [[R6-H5]]|<ref name="Lair of Grievous" />}}
[[File:Vassek_system.png|thumb|left|280px|The Vassek system, the star system in which Vassek 3 was located]]
Vassek 3, otherwise known as the third [[moon]] of [[Vassek]], was one of three moons that [[orbit]]ed the [[planet]] Vassek in the [[star system]] of the [[Vassek system|same name]], located within the [[Wazta sector]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="BMF 65" /> and the [[Western Reaches]].<ref name="WesternReaches" /> Situated in grid square I-17 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]], the moon had a standard [[Gravity|gravitational]] pull<ref name="BMF 65" /> as well as a breathable, Type I [[atmosphere]],<ref name="Atmosphere" /> which provided tolerable conditions for most of [[the galaxy]]'s [[oxygen]]-breathing beings. Vassek 3 and the rest of the Vassek system were located far enough off the [[Koda Spur]] [[hyperspace route]] that the moon did not receive many visitors.<ref name="BMF 65" />

The moon was shrouded in dense, perpetual mists and possessed no signs of [[Plant|vegetation]] larger than [[lichen]]s. Its fogs also obscured the view of the moon's surface from [[Realspace|space]], with only glimpses of the satellite's rocky landscape permitted by breaks in the mists. Furthermore, attempting to land on Vassek 3's surface was difficult as a result of the moon's vapors, which forced [[pilot]]s to utilize scanning equipment and [[sensor]] systems to locate suitable landing areas.<ref name="BMF 65" /> Vassek 3's landscape was marked by craggy, [[moss]]-covered, and fog-filled canyons<ref name="Episode Guide" /> as well as sharp, towering<ref name="BMF 65" /> rocky<ref name="Episode Guide" /> [[mountain]]s, plunging gorges, and tall columns.<ref name="BMF 65" />

==History==
===Fortress of General Grievous===
{{Quote|Don't worry, Ahsoka, we'll catch Gunray yet.|Kit Fisto, to [[Ahsoka Tano]]|<ref name="Lair of Grievous" />}}
Sometime during the [[Clone Wars]] between the [[Galactic Republic]] and [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], the [[Kaleesh]] Separatist [[General]] [[Grievous]] constructed a personal [[Grievous's fortress|fortress]] on the surface of Vassek 3.<ref name="Build R2 57">{{BuildR2Cite|57|Droid Directory}}</ref> Throughout the war, the fortress was utilized as Grievous's place of rest between battles<ref name="Rise">''[[Rise of the Separatists]]''</ref> as well as his safe haven and the location where he would receive repairs for his [[cybernetics]] when they became damaged in battle.<ref name="Build R2 57" />

[[File:Syliure-31Hyperdrive-SWZ.png|thumb|right|280px|Kit Fisto arrives at Vassek 3.]]
In [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{TCWcanondates|110}}</ref> [[Jedi General]] [[Kit Fisto]] [[Mission to Grievous's castle|traveled]] to the Vassek system in search of [[Trade Federation]] [[Viceroy]] [[Nute Gunray]], who had previously [[Rescue on the Tranquility|escaped]] Republic custody through the assistance of Separatist forces. Locating the [[Homing beacon|tracking beacon]] from a Republic [[Consular-class cruiser (Charger c70 retrofit)|vessel]] utilized in Gunray's supposed escape to Vassek's third moon, Fisto landed on the moon in his [[Kit Fisto's Delta-7B starfighter|personal]] [[Delta-7B Aethersprite-class light interceptor|starfighter]]. After landing, Fisto became reunited with his former [[Padawan]], [[Jedi Knight]] [[Nahdar Vebb]], and a [[Fil's Squad|detachment]] of [[clone trooper]]s led by [[Clone Commander]] [[Fil]], who had arrived on the natural satellite in a [[Nu-class attack/transport shuttle|Republic shuttle]].<ref name="Lair of Grievous" />

===Encounter with the Republic===
{{Quote|Cooperate, Grievous, and perhaps the Senate will be merciful.''"<br />"''It is you who shall get no mercy.|Kit Fisto and Grievous|audio=NoMercy-LoG.flac|<ref name="Lair of Grievous" />}}
Fisto and the Republic [[task force]] unknowingly entered Grievous's fortress and continued their search for Gunray. While they moved through the citadel, the Jedi and the [[trooper]]s overheard the viceroy relaying orders to several [[B1-series battle droid]]s. The Jedi destroyed the [[Battle droid|droids]] shortly thereafter but discovered that Gunray had been speaking through a [[hologram]]. In the transmission, Gunray was then replaced by the Confederate [[Head of State]], [[Count]] [[Dooku]], who proceeded to offer the Republic an alternative target in the viceroy's place&mdash;Grievous, who, as the task force then learned, owned the citadel and had presently arrived in Vassek 3's orbit. Fisto, Vebb, and the [[Cloning|clone]] troopers then began to prepare a trap in order to capture the general.<ref name="Lair of Grievous" />

[[File:FistoSurpise.png|thumb|left|280px|Grievous is ambushed by a Republic task force in his personal fortress.]]
As Grievous entered the citadel, Fisto and the rest of the task force revealed themselves and demanded that Grievous surrender. In response, the general engaged the Jedi and their troopers in combat, [[Death|killing]] several of the clones while also taking damage to his cybernetics, forcing him to retreat in order to receive repairs from his [[EV-series medical droid|medical droid]], [[EV-A4-D]]. Following his repairs, as well as the death of Commander Fil at the hands of the general's pet [[roggwart]], [[Gor]]&mdash;who was in turn killed by Fisto&mdash;Grievous exited his command center and [[Lightsaber duel|fought]] and killed Vebb. Following his former Padawan's death, the Jedi Master began to make his escape from the moon but was briefly confronted by Grievous in Vassek 3's mists. Despite the Separatist general's efforts, however, Fisto was able to escape into his [[starfighter]] and withdraw from the moon as the sole survivor of the mission.<ref name="Lair of Grievous" /> Sometime after Grievous chased the Jedi from the moon, the general abandoned his fortress and relocated elsewhere in the galaxy,<ref name="HC 64">{{HelmetCollectionCite|64|Databank A-Z}}</ref> repairing his destroyed doctor as well,<ref name="Build R2-D2 53">{{BuildR2Cite|53|Droid Directory}}</ref> since the Republic had found the location of his base.<ref name="HC 64" /> A [[Unidentified historical book|book]] describing objects relating to [[Timeline of galactic history|galactic history]] included an entry on Grievous' mask, which mentioned the warlord's fortress on the moon.<ref name="100 Objects">''[[Star Wars 100 Objects]]''</ref>

==Locations==
{{Quote|This place looks like a shrine to that strange warrior.|Kit Fisto, on Grievous's statues|<ref name="Lair of Grievous" />}}
Hidden within a mountain on Vassek 3 was the personal fortress of General Grievous, who returned to the citadel between Clone Wars engagements for rest and repairs to his cybernetic [[limb]]s. The looming fortress was a depressing and gloomy structure filled with deadly traps<ref name="BMF 65" /> and also served as the home of Gor, the general's roggwart pet. The fortress was protected by several [[IG-100 MagnaGuard]] droids and maintained by at least five B1-series battle [[droid]]s and Grievous's EV-series [[medical droid]], EV-A4-D, who was responsible for carrying out any repairs on Grievous's damaged cybernetics.<ref name="Lair of Grievous" />

==Behind the scenes==
Vassek 3 was introduced in the opening newsreel of "[[Rookies (episode)|Rookies]],"<ref name="Rookies">{{TCW|Rookies (episode)}}</ref> the fifth episode of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' television series' [[The Clone Wars: Season One|first season]], which aired on [[October 24]], [[2008]].<ref name="Rookies Ep Guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode005.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Rookies}}</ref> The moon later made its first proper appearance in "[[Lair of Grievous]],"<ref name="Lair of Grievous" /> the first season's tenth episode, which aired on [[December 12]], 2008.<ref name="Lair of Grievous Ep Guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode010.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Lair of Grievous}}</ref>

In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], Vassek 3 was identified in the [[2017]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''.<ref name="TVE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> The [[2023]] reference book ''[[Star Wars 100 Objects]]'' referred to the moon as simply "Vassek."<ref name="100 Objects" /> In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, the [[StarWars.com]] [[The Clone Wars Episode Guides|episode guide]] for "Lair of Grievous" identified the natural satellite as the [[Third moon of Vassek/Legends|third moon of Vassek]].<ref name="Lair of Grievous Ep Guide" />

